    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Step 1 — which instance?",
      "prov:value": "The\nsimulator directory was the literal `folio-assistant/simulators` until it\nbecame a config field; the Lake prefix was `QOU.` until it was read from\n`lakefile.toml`, and is now left **unprefixed** when no lakefile names one,\nbecause a wrong namespace is worse than none."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Step 2 — which declared graph, and where does that instance put it?",
      "prov:value": "A declared-but-absent directory is worse than\n  an undeclared one: every consumer scans nothing and reports a clean run over\n  it (bean `dh4f`, thirty pipeline scripts, three of them passing over a corpus\n  they could not read).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dh4f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The `docs` graph, and the filing question it answers",
      "prov:value": "`docs` is an authorable destination like the others, and it is the one an agent\nmost often forgets to consider — measured 2026-09-21, when this agent derived\nthe destination list for a CRDM sign-off straight from the declaration and\nstill **omitted `docs`**, offering skill / proposal / nothing for a design\nrecord that belonged in none of them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The `docs` graph, and the filing question it answers",
      "prov:value": "**WHOSE `docs/` comes first, and it is Step 1's question again.** Owner,\n2026-09-21: *\"if it is realated to some harness/feature/tool that detailed\ninfromation/design/planning/etc go into that harness' docs/\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The `docs` graph, and the filing question it answers",
      "prov:value": "A record written in the\n   present tense becomes a claim about today, and goes stale invisibly — the\n   `8nzu` failure, where a dated observation read as current guidance.\n2."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The `docs` graph, and the filing question it answers",
      "prov:value": "**The line between the two, stated as a test** — the owner's, 2026-09-21:\n\n> **A skill carries what a competent practitioner needs IN ORDER TO DO the\n> task. Anything beyond that is documentation.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The inheritance gap — know it before you rely on it",
      "prov:value": "`resolveSkillDirs` in `schemas/kg/harness-config.ts`\ncomputes the cross-instance skill overlay and **has no caller**, so skill\ndiscovery is **root-only in practice today** and a dependency's skills are not\nyet reachable. Outstanding Phase 0.1 work."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Step 3 — which KIND of node?",
      "prov:value": "**Actor / role / skill / permission is the one with a measured cost.** One\nsentence carries the model — *an actor performs a task in a process as a role,\nusing that role's skills* — and moving permissions onto Role, which looks right,\nproduced **36 conflicts** where a permission was held by some but not all actors\nsharing a role."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The agent-file stub — a pointer, never a home",
      "prov:value": "A rule that exists only in `AGENTS.md` is not in the generated\n  reference, not in the published skill docs, and not found by an agent that\n  went looking for the skill first. The turn-report discipline lived there\n  alone until it was moved."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The artefact stub — resolve it, never compose it",
      "prov:value": "The graph document is under the instance's own directory, the host's\nincluded (owner, 2026-10-23: one rule for every layer, with subjects beside\ntheir document;\n[`instance-publication`](instance-publication.md) §\"Which base an `@id` is\nminted against\").",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The artefact stub — resolve it, never compose it",
      "prov:value": "The knowledge-graph tile in the site\nnavbar was hand-written as `/kg/` and **404'd from the day it was added** —\nnothing has ever been published there, because the real path comes out of\n`renderingPath`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/placement.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The worked failure this skill exists to prevent",
      "prov:value": "`scripts/generate-readme.sh` lived in the **platform** and ended in\n`cp \"$OUT\" README.md`."
    }
  ]
